# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Detailed description of the impact of this finding.
LeverageZapRouterBase._openCdpOperation() allows a user to flashloan and then open a CDP using the loaned stETH. There is postcheck to ensure that the cdp.coll is no less than a certain amount. However, due the the wrong comparison operator, it ensure the other way around: it will ensure that  cdp.coll is not more than a certain amount instead. 


## Proof of Concept
Provide direct links to all referenced code in GitHub. Add screenshots, logs, or any other relevant proof that illustrates the concept.

First, LeverageZapRouterBase._openCdpOperation() allows a user to flashloan and then open a CDP using the loaned stETH. There is postcheck to ensure that the cdp.coll is no less than a certain amount.

[https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-badger/blob/9173558ee1ac8a78a7ae0a39b97b50ff0dd9e0f8/ebtc-zap-router/src/LeverageZapRouterBase.sol#L185-L192](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-badger/blob/9173558ee1ac8a78a7ae0a39b97b50ff0dd9e0f8/ebtc-zap-router/src/LeverageZapRouterBase.sol#L185-L192)

However, LeverageZapRouterBase._getPostCheckParams() uses the comparison operator ```Operator.gte``` instead of ```Operator.lte```. This is wrong since it will make a comparison like ```check.value >= cdp.coll``` where ```check.value``` is the minimum expected collateral amount and cdp.coll is the collateral shares of the cdp.

[https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-badger/blob/9173558ee1ac8a78a7ae0a39b97b50ff0dd9e0f8/ebtc-zap-router/src/LeverageZapRouterBase.sol#L257-L274](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-badger/blob/9173558ee1ac8a78a7ae0a39b97b50ff0dd9e0f8/ebtc-zap-router/src/LeverageZapRouterBase.sol#L257-L274)

Second, the post check will ba made like this: 

[https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-badger/blob/9173558ee1ac8a78a7ae0a39b97b50ff0dd9e0f8/ebtc-protocol/packages/contracts/contracts/LeverageMacroBase.sol#L207-L216](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-badger/blob/9173558ee1ac8a78a7ae0a39b97b50ff0dd9e0f8/ebtc-protocol/packages/contracts/contracts/LeverageMacroBase.sol#L207-L216)

where _doCheckValueType() is implemented like this: 

[https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-badger/blob/9173558ee1ac8a78a7ae0a39b97b50ff0dd9e0f8/ebtc-protocol/packages/contracts/contracts/LeverageMacroBase.sol#L277-L290])https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-badger/blob/9173558ee1ac8a78a7ae0a39b97b50ff0dd9e0f8/ebtc-protocol/packages/contracts/contracts/LeverageMacroBase.sol#L277-L290)

Therefore, it won't ensure that the cdp.coll is no less than the specified minimum. 

Finally, our POC confirms my finding: 

1) we set collValidationBufferBPS, that is coll.coll is expected to be at least 
```_totalCollateral * _collValidationBuffer / BPS,```. 

2) check.value: 24502627687937533654, cdp.coll is expected to be no less than check.value

3) cdpInfo.coll: 25592239671513193321

4) Although we have cdpInfo.coll >= check.value, the check still fails due to the wrong direction of the comparison operator. 

